    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "in this example: https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/search?l=TypeScript&q=major&type=Code there are two `@Major` tags which have been there for 8 months (way before v4 release). \r\n\r\nSo although `@Major` was added we didn't include it in the v4. This means either:\r\n1. `@Major` should be removed for from those places and should never have been set\r\n2. `@Major` is not very effective in marking theses kind of changes.\r\n\r\nIf it's 2., I'm questioning the effectivity and the scaling of this process. A more effective approach would be to make a PR and merge it in a v5 branch. It's much better than building up an invisible pile of work that adds up to your next release. ",
    "commit_id": "fac827f503c96e4f0a05fcee50af9a49e39bb4bc",
